Hi,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve been trying to create a tabsetPanel which depends on some sidebar inputs, avoiding conditionalPanels, by using renderUI and a function to generate the tabPanel code. I gathered from <a href="https://groups.google.com/d/msg/shiny-discuss/-xSng1348MU/MW3qxNUoFEwJ" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msg/shiny-discuss/-xSng1348MU/MW3qxNUoFEwJ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792408887198000&amp;usg=AOvVaw03UfGnKOJSEZ468Q0Bs2SS">a post last month</a> that it might be possible but I can&#39;t seem to work it! What I have looks roughly like this:</div><div><br></div><div>server.R:</div><div><br></div><div><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px"><div>output$theTabset &lt;- renderUI({</div></blockquote></div><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px"><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px"><div><div>theOutputs &lt;- returnOutputs(input1, input2, input3)</div></div></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px"><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px"><div>tabsetPanel(</div></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px"><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px"><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px"><div>theOutputs</div></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px"><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px"><div> )</div></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px"><div> })</div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>ui.R:</div><div><br></div><div><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px"><div>mainPanel(</div></blockquote></div><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px"><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px"><div><div>... </div></div></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px"><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px"><div><div>uiOutput(&quot;theTabset&quot;),</div></div></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px"><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px"><div>...</div></blockquote></blockquote><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px"><div>)</div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>The output of returnOutputs() is a list with each element being the HTML for a tabPanel:</div><div><br></div><div><div>&gt; returnOutputs(1,1,1)</div><div>[[1]]</div><div>[1] &quot;&lt;div class=\&quot;tab-pane\&quot; title=\&quot;Panel 1\&quot;&gt;
  &lt;div id=\&quot;panel1Table\&quot; class=\&quot;shiny-html-output\&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div id=\&quot;npanel1Plot\&quot; class=\&quot;shiny-plot-output\&quot; style=\&quot;width: 90% ; height: 500px\&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&quot;</div><div>attr(,&quot;html&quot;)</div><div>[1] TRUE</div><div><br></div><div>[[2]]</div><div>[1] &quot;&lt;div class=\&quot;tab-pane\&quot; title=\&quot;Panel 2\&quot;&gt;
  &lt;div id=\&quot;panel2Table\&quot; class=\&quot;shiny-html-output\&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div id=\&quot;npanel1Plot\&quot; class=\&quot;shiny-plot-output\&quot; style=\&quot;width: 90% ; height: 500px\&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&quot;</div><div>attr(,&quot;html&quot;)</div><div>[1] TRUE</div></div><div><br></div><div>and I&#39;ve defined output$panel1Table, output$panel1Plot, etc. in server.R.</div><div><br></div><div>Everything except the tabsetPanel renders fine, but I get an error:</div><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px"><div>Error in if (!grepl(pattern, text)) return(text) : </div></blockquote><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px"><blockquote style="margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px"><div>  argument is of length zero</div></blockquote></blockquote><div>and no tabsetPanel.</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve also tried changing output$theTabset to exclude the tabsetPanel( ) part in server.R and just return theOutputs, and having uiOutput(&quot;theTabset&quot;) inside a tabsetPanel in ui.R, but that was even less successful.</div><div><br></div><div>Does anyone know any solutions to this?</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div>Ben</div>
